{
  "abstract": "A preprint of 30 Sep 2026 (OpenAI; not refereed) claims HC and GHC for all powers of K3 surfaces whose transcendental space embeds in V_P = (U^2 + <-1>^4)_Q. Its only lattice-specific input is a six-parameter family of double covers of abelian surfaces, attached to a character of order 4, whose eigenspace is a K3-type variation with form V_P and full period rank. Replacing the character by one of order 6 and taking the two-dimensional S_3-isotypic piece gives a rank-8 K3-type variation with period map of rank 6 and form V_3 = (U^2 + <-1,-1,-3,-3>)_Q, which has Hasse invariant -1 exactly at 3 and infinity. We check each lattice-specific step of the preprint for this seed. Conditional on its general sections, HC and GHC follow for all powers of every projective K3 surface with T embedding in V_3. A rank-6 Witt-index-1 space embeds in V_3 iff its obstruction primes lie in {3}. This covers 22 of the 33 index-1 elliptic types in the census of rStation hodge_conjecture_23, and 31 of 33 together with V_P. We prove that seeds of this type with cyclic isogeny never give K3-type pieces of rank above 8. An untwisted (1,3) seed has a rank-10 piece of form U^2 + <-1>^6, which would cover every rational K3-type space of rank at most 7. We explain why the preprint's curve domination fails there, conditional on full signed Weyl monodromy of the Gauss tower, which is supported numerically but not proved.",
